The patch of the AppRun of nix-appimage (`appruns/userns-chroot/main.c`, rev 28b2101). Refer to
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §11 and `docs/DISCUSSION.md` §30.

The AppRun shows the store of the AppImage at `/nix/store`. First, it tries an overlay of the store of the image
and the store of the system. A system that is not NixOS has no `/nix/store`, so the overlay fails. Then the AppRun
binds a folder of the image onto `/nix/store`. Without this patch, it binds `<appdir>/nix`, not `<appdir>/nix/store`.
Thus, each path becomes `/nix/store/store/<hash>-...`, and the start fails with "No such file or directory".

This patch binds `<appdir>/nix/store`. The overlay on NixOS does not change.

--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@
 	const char* nix_in_mountroot = strprintf("%s/nix", mountroot);
 	die_if(mkdir(nix_in_mountroot, 0777) < 0, "mkdir %s", nix_in_mountroot);
 
-	const char* nix_from = strprintf("%s/nix", appdir);
+	const char* nix_from = strprintf("%s/nix/store", appdir);
 	const char* nix_to = strprintf("%s/nix/store", mountroot);
 	die_if(mkdir(nix_to, 0777) < 0, "mkdir %s", nix_to);
 
